WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:05.640
Do you have any texts from anyone that has passed away?

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.640
Yeah.

00:00:12.769 --> 00:00:14.629
So, she sent me...

00:00:14.629 --> 00:00:16.989
she sent me like this picture of her,

00:00:17.599 --> 00:00:22.389
she said 'Currently on an IV', I said 'geez' and she said 'Did a flu swab on me?

00:00:22.419 --> 00:00:27.488
I have pneumonia' I said 'From vaping those weed pens. Hope you don't have that vaping disease'

00:00:27.949 --> 00:00:31.238
She said 'No, I don't it's pneumonia and I'm done with pens'

00:00:31.879 --> 00:00:33.410
and then...

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.739
My dad called me that she was in surgery on Friday...

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.800
Emergency surgery...I-

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:42.579
And it wasn't looking good. I texted her: 'I love you' and

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:45.610
And she died before she could read that.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.140
So...

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:55.869
Three months later. We got the autopsy report back and it was associated with electronic cigarette use.

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:04.480
I do have one from my mom...who passed away, um

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:06.720
August 31st 2019

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:15.400
Actually, I don't know what it was regarding. She just messaged me randomly. She said 'We need to talk' and

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:21.600
For some reason like I'd seen it, but I didn't respond and I said the next day: 'yes'

00:01:23.209 --> 00:01:25.069
So, I...

00:01:25.069 --> 00:01:27.069
don't know what it was about, but

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:34.960
me and my mom, we don't really have the best relationship. We didn't, um, she was...

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:39.100
heavily involved in like drug and alcohol, so she couldn't take care of me and she was she

00:01:39.829 --> 00:01:47.049
gave me to my grandparents really to you know, raise me and I was just so bitter and so like

00:01:47.869 --> 00:01:52.898
frustrated and so like why would you do that? I'm your son.

00:01:52.898 --> 00:01:54.619
Let me get it. Um,

00:01:54.619 --> 00:01:56.619
So...

00:01:56.899 --> 00:01:58.899
Um...it's from my best friend,

00:01:59.329 --> 00:02:00.829
and I said

00:02:00.829 --> 00:02:06.788
'Yo so why'd you deactivate? I was gonna ask you if you wanted to come live with me in Idaho

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:08.799
or at least stay here for a while.'

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.630
Umm...and she

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:16.040
said 'I would love that why the sudden ask'

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:19.900
I don't know honestly it would just be fun if you came here.'

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:26.400
Yeah, she passed away 20 days after that...

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.420
In the end, it was because she uh c-committed suicide.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:38.240
My-my friend Stan, I mean, I don't know if I had anything to do with him being Hawaiian

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:42.839
but he's just the most chill laid-back dude. Early last year, he was uh, yeah

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:48.240
He'd like Stage four lymphoma. And I said, 'How are you feeling Stan?' And he says 'I'm doing well

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:53.140
I'm going to stay one more day. I have an appointment tomorrow with my oncologist

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.120
thank you for praying for me. God is good.'

00:02:56.130 --> 00:03:03.299
'Try to comfort your mom for she's under a lot of stress.' -'Sounds good Stan. I will be here for my mom as well

00:03:03.370 --> 00:03:09.240
Thank you for caring for her. We'll continue to pray for you.' And he said 'thanks.' We're at the hospital with him

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:11.200
literally

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:17.640
as he was taking his last breaths, and I was like 'You're about to go home right now ', you know and

00:03:18.040 --> 00:03:20.639
And I was just like 'Man, I'm excited for you.'

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.640
I, remember after she died,

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:25.280
I called my sister umm...

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:29.220
He was at the hospital and I remember telling her like 'oh my god,

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:34.020
I don't remember the last time I told my mom "I love you"', and she said 'Me either'

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.760
So, I would really love to tell her that again

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:45.480
Definitely a lot more now and I call them and I text them way more often, obviously

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:51.140
Since I didn't really get to talk to my mom too much and I really regret that now but yeah

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:54.720
I call them like every week. -I still send messages to her

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:57.810
on Instagram because...

00:03:58.209 --> 00:04:04.859
Her family didn't deactivate the account. 'I miss you.' 'I feel so alone without you.'

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.200
'I don't know what I'm doing'

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.100
...and then I said

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:18.809
'Why didn't you say goodbye before you left?' and then another message was...'I love you'

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:22.650
Sorry...

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:31.519
She was sending like messages, like audio messages and I'll just play one 'cause...

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.520
I don't know, see...

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.320
I wanna tell you,

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:39.880
that...umm, I'll be done with school
in about 12 months...

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.519
so, then I get my license

00:04:41.519 --> 00:04:45.100
So that is the doctor, and the therapist

00:04:45.100 --> 00:04:47.100
So, one more year...that's it.

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.100
Just hold on...

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:50.400
But,

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.900
You can see me in 25, if you need to.

00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.100
Just be consistent...

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.760
Love you, son.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.100
(exhales deeply)

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.840
And that's...

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:11.060
(clears throat) that's the last time I heard her voice,

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:13.900
and...

00:05:14.129 --> 00:05:20.389
It was, I don't know...I found out that she passed away

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.800
the day of and

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:25.889
everything just like...

00:05:25.889 --> 00:05:30.468
came at once like, the regret. I just feel like, I should have like...

00:05:31.979 --> 00:05:39.619
...done way more than I did and this sucks because I can never physically say I'm sorry. You know,

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:43.699
just apologize for just ignoring you for so many years and...

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:46.580
just not...

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:48.569
understanding your story.

00:05:48.569 --> 00:05:52.878
Like I-I'm pretty sure she understand mine.

00:05:52.878 --> 00:05:53.849
My dad...

00:05:53.849 --> 00:05:58.249
had to go in for like an emergency surgery over like his two years of having cancer,

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:01.369
he eventually like lost his ability to speak.

00:06:01.379 --> 00:06:08.929
And...so the main way we like communicated was through text or like through writing and it was a really tough transition home.

00:06:09.389 --> 00:06:13.278
We were like trying to get him settled in to his house and his room

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:15.449
knowing that like eventually that was

00:06:15.449 --> 00:06:21.318
where he was gonna be until he passed and then he finally was like awake so I popped into his room just to say like

00:06:21.319 --> 00:06:23.319
Hey, like, I'm leaving now. So...

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:27.469
as I was leaving, he texted me and he said

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:32.599
'Hi taylor, thank you for being there for me. It means a lot to me. love you'

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:40.249
And he's...my dad is never like super affectionate.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.300
So, yeah, I think like him...

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:50.900
For me, like knowing that he

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.960
...went out of his way to like text that to me and

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:56.100
...was

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.100
appreciative that I was there,

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:06.770
was really touching to me. He knew that his time was short and I knew, so yeah that text means a lot to me.

